erican intelligence says I believe  Putin at least on the issue of  Korea's weapons capabilities number two  Trump's refusal to enforce sanctions  that are in the law against Russia and  the reversal of existing sanctions  Donald Trump has done both we told you  recently that Donald Trump is ending the  joint nuclear agreement which opens the  door to Russia further arming itself  does it matter whether Trump thinks he's  doing it because it's better for America  or because he's doing it because it's  good for Putin if it's good for Putin  and if it's good for Russia then Trump  is assisting them in what they want to  have happen number four multiple lies  about Donald Trump's interests in Russia  even if Trump is lying out of stupidity  about the extent to which Trump Tower  Moscow was being explored it's still  good for Russia that Donald Trump  appears to be evasive and dishonest  about it because it simply raises more  questions about why that's good for  Russia number five or maybe six at this  point I don't know I'm losing track  Trump's threats to pull out of NATO even  if Trump has reasons that he believes  are good reasons to pull out of NATO  that have nothing to do with Russia that  plays directly into the Russian priority  of destabilizing NATO causing chaos in  the geopolitical West number six or  seven withdrawal from Syria withdrawal  from Syria is counter to what every  relevant expert says make sense in the  way that Trump is proposing it still  hasn't happened by the way it's not  clear if it will but it plays directly  into Russian geopolitical priorities so  at this point Pat this is not defensible  period the only argument there is is one  over whether Trump is knowingly doing  this stuff to benefit Russia or whether  he believes that he has his own reasons  and it just happens to be exactly what  Russia wants him to do I think that  Trump being a Russian asset makes a lot  more sense than him being a Russian  agent I just don't think he's smart  enough to be a Russian agent he would  accidentally admit to it on national TV  like how he admitted to Lester Holt that  he fired James Comey over the Russia  investigation or  how he admitted recently that he didn't  have to declare a national emergency I  don't think he can think that many moves  ahead and I think that he is being  manipulated but he doesn't fully know it  yeah at minimum we have an unambiguous  series of events that show Donald Trump  is betraying American interests in the  favor of Russia and the extent to which  this is coordinated puppeteering by  Russia or not we just don't know we may  never know and most importantly and I'm  going to be going back to this a lot in  the coming what is it 11 9 28 21 months  I guess it is until the election Donald  Trump may well get reelected in 2020  which would be an indictment not just on  Trump voters but also on anti Trump  voters who choose to stay home and I  know that I'm going to get emails saying  David you really shouldn't be  preemptively blaming people who don't  like Trump I'm not what I'm saying is  when 50% of the country doesn't vote if  Donald Trump gets reelected it's not  just because his base supports him it's  also because not enough people who don't  support Trump voted it's just a  mathematical reality and it's a very  plausible reality not probable I won't  say at this point but it's a very  plausible reality that Donald Trump will  indeed be reelected we have a poll out  right now on YouTube and Instagram  asking what are you going to use as  information to evaluate who you will  vote for in the 2020 Democratic primary  you can find this on the YouTube  community tab as well as on the David  Pakman show  Instagram page which is at David Pakman  show participate boat and we will have  results hopefully for you tomorrow  today's program is sponsored in part by  spresso bucks who are offering everybody  in our audience a bunch of really cool  free stuff suppressor Vox is a company  b